{"step_index":321,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T15:42:11Z","content":"### How It Works:\n\nIn modern mobile architecture, **we do not store raw multi-megabyte image binary blobs directly inside SQLite tables** (as that would bloat the database file and degrade query performance). \n\nInstead, the app uses a **Persistent Local File Storage + SQLite Pointer Architecture**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    IMAGE STORAGE & DATABASE ARCHITECTURE                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                             │\n│  1. Scanned Document Image (.jpg)                                           │\n│     • Saved permanently to device local storage (iOS / Android sandbox).    │\n│     • Persisted at: FileSystem.documentDirectory/scanned_sheets/...          │\n│                                                                             │\n│  2. SQLite Database Pointer (`source_image_uri`)                            │\n│     • Stored in the `lists` table:                                          │\n│       `source_image_uri = \"file:///var/mobile/.../sheet_1724.jpg\"`          │\n│                                                                             │\n│  3. The Image is PRESERVED, Not Discarded                                   │\n│     • The physical card photo remains permanently stored on your phone.     │\n│                                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Would you like a 1-Tap \"View Original Sheet\" Button in the HUD?\n\nSince the photo is permanently preserved, we can add a **\"View Original Report Card\"** button directly inside the **Power Dialer HUD** and **Lead Profile**. \n\nThis allows you to tap a single button while on a call to pop up a zoomable modal of the educator's original handwritten report card if you ever need to double-check their handwriting in real-time. \n\nWould you like me to enable that button in the HUD?","thinking":"**Investigating Storage Strategy**\n\nOkay, I'm digging into the codebase. Currently, it seems the focus is on a database table called 'lists', and the schema includes text-based data but not the images themselves. This suggests the application isn't directly saving the image files.\n\n\n"}
